# A type an owner ships (docs/extensions.md, "Owners and types, as built"). csv-table, installed
# in the empty home by tests/drive.rs, ships csv-table.row in its manifest for the CSV rows none
# of the workspace's types matches: Volcanoes/Observatories.csv's rows, which it gives as row
# pieces, are csv-table.row, while Eruptions.csv's stay eruptions, which the workspace's own
# type matches by their columns.
size 140x30
env COLD_LAVA_EDITOR=none
wait-for example-workspace
keys /
type vesuvius
wait-for Vesuvius
keys enter
# csv-table has read the CSV: its row links to Vesuvius.
wait-for ← Observatories.csv
keys esc esc
wait-for cold-lava workspaces
keys i
wait-for csv-table.row        3
expect eruption             8
type csv-table
wait-for rows · /csv-table
keys enter
wait-for 3 rows
expect Hawaiian Volcano Observatory  Kīlauea
expect-not Krakatoa
screen
# Its name is the row's first cell, read by a pattern over the row's words. A piece's words are
# not the type's to rewrite, so the table refuses and says why, and tests/drive.rs reads the CSV
# unchanged. A cell is set in csv-table's own table, or through a type that reads its column by
# name (csv-edit.drive).
keys e
wait-for name: Vesuvius Observatory▏
keys ctrl+u
type Osservatorio Vesuviano
keys enter
wait-for not saved: name of a csv-table.row is read from what a piece doesn't hold as a value
keys esc
wait-for cold-lava workspaces
keys q
exits 0
